{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/863791-are-dragon-blooded-of-a-different-color-still-a-thing","id":863791,"title":"Are \"Dragon-Blooded of a Different Color\" still a thing?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-11T11:29:47-07:00","id":863791,"title":"Are \"Dragon-Blooded of a Different Color\" still a thing?","content":"Will there still be Dragon-Blooded that are all ghostly and such still be a thing in 3E. I always enjoyed them in 2E <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/687-cydoc","name":"Cydoc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T11:38:13-07:00","id":863795,"title":"","content":"Nothing has been stated in the core book. I feel like a dev said something about them in the past, but I have no quotes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T11:47:16-07:00","id":863798,"title":"","content":"Nothing has really been said about necromancy at all, and that was their primary feature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T11:52:09-07:00","id":863801,"title":"","content":"One thing that the devs <i>have</i> given their pronouncement on is that they support *-blooded Exalts, like Demon-Blooded Solars; so even if dark-DBs aren't coming back, you can still have something pretty similar with Ghost-Blooded DBs, allowing them to initiate into Necromancy.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if we even know that DBs <i>can't</i> initiate into necromancy in the new edition, since Sorcery (and by extension Necromancy) has changed so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T11:52:31-07:00","id":863802,"title":"","content":"I think necromancy has been mentioned as just being another sorcerous initiation, so it seems logical that nothing except culture would prevent a Dragon-Blood from learning it. The other differences were basically fluff (mostly what your anima looked like, iirc?), so there's not likely to be anything preventing you from having a Dragon of a Different Color or even a whole clan of them if you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T11:56:17-07:00","id":863805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Guancyto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/863791-are-dragon-blooded-of-a-different-color-still-a-thing?p=863802#post863802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think necromancy has been mentioned as just being another sorcerous initiation</div> </div> </div> </div>Has it? I remember the possibility of it being discussed amongst the forum, but I don't remember any devs/writers confirming either way.<br /> <br /> While it makes little difference in terms of Workings, since they're all unique to the character, it does make at least a small difference in terms of the Spells you'd have access to.<br /> <br /> Though I guess the argument could be made that spell access doesn't really matter since the real focus is character thematics anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T12:02:16-07:00","id":863809,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm using them regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T12:37:55-07:00","id":863831,"title":"","content":"Excellent, thanks for the responses","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/687-cydoc","name":"Cydoc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T14:43:48-07:00","id":863907,"title":"","content":"So far, considering that all we have on Necromancy in 3e is one sample nephwrack antagonist, some fluff tidbits and lots of forum talk, i would guess it's overall wait and see.<br /> <br /> They might be an option still, rendered unnecessary rules changes that make necromancy more accessible to non-abyssals (the &quot;Necromancy is just a peculiar initiation in sorcery&quot; option being one such possible venue) or made a viable concept alternative along with vitriol-touched terrestrials, gossamer-blooded, autochtonian dragons or who knows what other weird options. Time will tell and if the books don't give them to us such beings, they will most probably give us the tools to brew our own ideas and takes of these if need be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T15:27:12-07:00","id":863935,"title":"","content":"I feel like there's elements of Dragons of a Different Color, or at least dark and twisted Dragon-Blooded in the city description for Gloam, fwiw. It gives grounds to start exploring that space, if nothing else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Pronounced &quot;Monkey Pie&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/762726-actual-play-the-party-prelude-project\" target=\"_blank\">Find my actual play content here!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/656-monkipi","name":"Monkipi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar656_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"318"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T15:30:33-07:00","id":863937,"title":"","content":"Association with necromancy might be a thing, but the name probably won't be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T17:51:29-07:00","id":863996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/863791-are-dragon-blooded-of-a-different-color-still-a-thing?p=863937#post863937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Association with necromancy might be a thing, but the name probably won't be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any reason why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T18:04:07-07:00","id":864001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/863791-are-dragon-blooded-of-a-different-color-still-a-thing?p=863996#post863996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any reason why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I claim to speak for Isator, but for me at least\u2026<br /> <br /> Felt kinda goofy, for one thing, for the setting to have come up with a common-use household name for a genetic anomaly when it's so rare that it has only occurred something like once or twice in living memory.<br /> <br /> Especially when their only significant difference is being able to learn necromancy instead of sorcery <i>when most DBs never learn sorcery <b>or</b> necromancy</i>.<br /> <br /> Especially especially when the Underworld has been so drastically retooled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-11-2016, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T23:06:58-07:00","id":864137,"title":"","content":"The presentation of Dragons of Another Colour was this weird middle ground between allowing a Dragon-Blooded Necromancer and shamelessly pandering to the notion of Abyssal Dragon-Blooded that resonate with the Elements of the Underworld in a manner that I don\u2019t think really satisfied either side.<br /> <br /> In 3e the Dynastic (or Lookshyan) Necromancer doesn\u2019t really gain from it being a rare genetic anomaly, the number of Dragon-Blooded who have an aptitude for sorcery and specifically choose to look to the Underworld or its denizens for enlightenment is going to be low enough to not require additional restrictions. You have weird and heretical powers much like you\u2019d get if you had secret liaisons with Mara or some creepy Sorcerous Relic that burrowed under your skin when it first came into your possession.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile if you want Dragon-Blooded tainted with <b>the power of death </b>then you can be a little more ambitious than giving them access to necromancy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T01:13:52-07:00","id":864174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/863791-are-dragon-blooded-of-a-different-color-still-a-thing?p=863996#post863996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any reason why?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a silly name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T01:24:31-07:00","id":864177,"title":"","content":"For 3e, it would totally be possible to have Dragon of a Different Color be a Dragon Blooded specific necromancy initiation. I doubt it will get official word count as such, but it would be really easy to have it show up as an initiation with merits and shaping rituals that reflect some changed thematics and aesthetics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T01:38:41-07:00","id":864180,"title":"","content":"After what they did to open up sorcery, I'm hoping there's a few initiations to Necromancy.<br /> Death and the afterlife is just such an enormous conceptual space to work with that shackling the whole thing to the Neverborn and treating it like sorcery's evil cousin seems like an enormous disservice.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T09:23:45-07:00","id":864337,"title":"","content":"I really like Dragons of a Different Color. The Terrestrial Exalted have a strong theme of Purity, and the DDCs play into that in an interesting way. Before I explain that, I want to clarify that &quot;Purity&quot; as a theme does not mean &quot;Eugenics and Nazis&quot; or even &quot;Racist Uncle at Thanksgiving&quot;. Instead, it refers to a cultural perception of what makes them superior (which a huge part of their religion explicitly says they are). The Terrestrial Exalted view themselves as a breed apart, a higher level of humanity worthy and deserving of obedience, respect and reverence. This stems from three different sources that are all distinct, but combine to form a single whole.<br /> First, they are spiritually superior. The Immaculate Philosophy states that the Dragon Blooded are humans whose souls are sufficiently pure that they deserve Exaltation, and are the only Exalted to achieve power from within rather than being granted power (Exigents) or stealing it (Anathema). This means that within their worldview, they are not people who Got Lucky and were placed into positions of power due to a privileged birth or arbitrary distinction. They are legitimately Better Than You down to their very souls, and questioning their place is petty jealousy at best and outright heresy at worst.<br /> Second, they have a direct bloodline connection to the Dragons. They almost certainly don't see this in a modern genetic sense, especially as there's no real reason to suppose that genetics works the same way in Exalted. However, they still view the expression of aspect markings as evidence of Purity in their blood, of a closeness to the Dragons that their power is of/from. The more spiritual among them would see this as a mark of favor, of a closeness to that distant ancestor that blesses them to emulate the Immaculate Dragons. The more pragmatic would see it as a sign of strength, of power. &quot;I am clearly marked by the Dragons, obey me&quot;. In either case, those with strong aspect markings would be favored, or at least looked upon as fortunate or blessed. They would be valued as marriage candidates - not because of any eugenics drive or genetic purity, but because it's useful to have someone like that as an ally.<br /> Third, they are descended from the Empress. Of course, not all of them are - Outcastes and Lost Eggs and such - but those that are can claim a connection to her power. In history, the children of Emperors or powerful merchant families or politicians are seen as just plain &quot;better&quot; than everyone else. They are a law apart, not because of any genetic greatness but because of their connections and bloodline. Most famous is probably the Borgia family, being children of the Pope let them get away with anything they wanted. This is the source of the Terrestrial hierarchy that sets Dynasts above Lost Eggs, a natural outcome of a society where who you know matters at least as much as whether you can set a farm on fire with your eyes.<br /> <br /> What does this have to do with Dragons of a Different Color? They challenge all three tenants of purity without invalidating them. A story with a DDC in it can use them to examine these cultural foundations in a way that few others can. The Immaculate Philosophy holds the underworld as a threat, ghosts are a moral failure, the hordes of the Dead worthy of a Wyld Hunt. Yet here are Terrestrial Exalted, no less powerful or moral or faithful than the rest, who have the markings of the Underworld. This is not an outright contradiction of course, but it could easily be a source of dissonance for a faithful Immaculate. How to reconcile an evil Underworld with a faithful Pyre Flame Aspect? You can turn to real world religions for inspiration here, for talk of noble suffering, of tested faith, of imperfect yet still worthy souls. To scorn the sin, but love the sinner. And what of their connection to the Elemental Dragons? Does a Void Aspect have the same connection that an Air Aspect does? How could such a perfect bloodline become corrupted? Does it reflect some weakness or illness within the Dragons themselves? And what of the more direct bloodline, that of the Empress? Does a DDC mean that your family has a ghost in its tree, an act condemned culturally and religiously? Were your parents cursed, perhaps, or did they bring it on themselves? There must naturally be suspicion that you are not a legitimate child, perhaps a ghostly lover or liaison in a shadowland? Whispers will follow you wherever you go, and any inheritance will surely be challenged by greedy siblings.<br /> <br /> In the end, their ability to perform necromancy is probably the least interesting aspect of Dragons of a Different Color. They will probably be more likely to learn it, due to cultural perception of DDCs as all necromancers and due to family pressure to learn a unique skill, but ultimately it's not more powerful than sorcery. Rather, it is the stories they enable that makes them so fascinating. Where do they come from? What do they mean? What is it like to be a theological question when you're just trying to be a person? How would a child or teenager cope with this scrutiny and pressure? These are questions that DDCs are especially - though not uniquely - suited to ask, and it's these questions that justify their inclusion in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/776-saintedphysician","name":"SaintedPhysician","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T09:34:21-07:00","id":864346,"title":"","content":"I head canon that Dragons of a Different Color didn't start showing up and were most numerous in the first few generations after the Contagion. In the Age of Sorrows, they are very rare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T10:06:09-07:00","id":864366,"title":"","content":"I think talking about Dragons of a Different Colour like they've got totally different Aspects to normal Dragon-Blooded highlights the unfortunate compromise I talked about.<br /> <br /> You talk about a <i>Bone Aspect</i> Dragon-Blooded and it sounds so weird and different, you're expecting someone like Marrow from the X-Men (or something kinkier) but then you meet a Wood Aspect whose Anima is rather spooky and feel massively ripped off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T10:10:52-07:00","id":864369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/863791-are-dragon-blooded-of-a-different-color-still-a-thing?p=864366#post864366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think talking about Dragons of a Different Colour like they've got totally different Aspects to normal Dragon-Blooded highlights the unfortunate compromise I talked about.<br /> <br /> You talk about a <i>Bone Aspect</i> Dragon-Blooded and it sounds so weird and different, you're expecting someone like Marrow from the X-Men (or something kinkier) but then you meet a Wood Aspect whose Anima is rather spooky and feel massively ripped off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which brings to mind the interesting bit that Liminals HAVE those aspects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T10:20:19-07:00","id":864380,"title":"","content":"Not quite, the only Underworld Element from First or Second Edition that Liminals have as one of their Aspects is Blood. I mean Marrow is pretty similar to Bone, but Flesh, Breath and Soil are pretty different from what we're familiar with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T11:25:00-07:00","id":864405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/863791-are-dragon-blooded-of-a-different-color-still-a-thing?p=864366#post864366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think talking about Dragons of a Different Colour like they've got totally different Aspects to normal Dragon-Blooded highlights the unfortunate compromise I talked about.<br /> <br /> You talk about a <i>Bone Aspect</i> Dragon-Blooded and it sounds so weird and different, you're expecting someone like Marrow from the X-Men (or something kinkier) but then you meet a Wood Aspect whose Anima is rather spooky and feel massively ripped off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems easy enough to fix. Add a keyword that makes certain Charms different for the dragons of the dead, give them a small number of unique Charms, and prohibit them from buying a certain subset of the normal Charmset.<br /> <br /> If bloodline Charms make it into the final release of the Terrestrial book, that'd be a natural model to work from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T12:07:57-07:00","id":864424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/863791-are-dragon-blooded-of-a-different-color-still-a-thing?p=864405#post864405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems easy enough to fix. Add a keyword that makes certain Charms different for the dragons of the dead, give them a small number of unique Charms, and prohibit them from buying a certain subset of the normal Charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because everyone liked the way Abyssals had mirror Solar charms plus a few of their own. If your going to make deathly DBs, you may as well make them their own splat than just trying to keyword your problem away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1236-loscabadrin","user":"Loscabadrin","date":". 04-12-2016, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1236-loscabadrin","name":"Loscabadrin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T12:33:56-07:00","id":864435,"title":"","content":"Was &quot;Dragons of a Different Color&quot; ever an in-setting term, or even a game-rules-term? Because so far as I remember it was just a cutesy title for a sidebar. We don't call Alchemicals who try to learn SMA &quot;Boom!, Revisiteds&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T12:35:36-07:00","id":864436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/863791-are-dragon-blooded-of-a-different-color-still-a-thing?p=864405#post864405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems easy enough to fix. Add a keyword that makes certain Charms different for the dragons of the dead, give them a small number of unique Charms, and prohibit them from buying a certain subset of the normal Charmset.<br /> <br /> If bloodline Charms make it into the final release of the Terrestrial book, that'd be a natural model to work from.</div> </div> </div> </div>The core problem I see is that you'd need to do the Underworld Elements justice thematically when they're not the most interesting thing in the world.<br /> <br /> Like Pyre Flame is only Fire in the most superficial of ways, its got more in common with Vitriol (especially when it's portrayed as being green when it feels like an interchangable substance) what does it do that's positive to justify the passion driven Fire Aspect ability spread? While we're thinking about this should a Pyre Flame Aspect even have the same ability spread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T12:37:08-07:00","id":864440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loscabadrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/863791-are-dragon-blooded-of-a-different-color-still-a-thing?p=864424#post864424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because everyone liked the way Abyssals had mirror Solar charms plus a few of their own. If your going to make deathly DBs, you may as well make them their own splat than just trying to keyword your problem away.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want a new splat. I just want DBs with a twist.<br /> <br /> Mirrors worked poorly because Abyssals were supposed to be a whole splat capable of standing on its own. If they were just a Solar variant of no particular setting significance, mirrors would've been a great idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T13:39:31-07:00","id":864497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/863791-are-dragon-blooded-of-a-different-color-still-a-thing?p=864440#post864440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't want a new splat. I just want DBs with a twist.<br /> <br /> Mirrors worked poorly because Abyssals were supposed to be a whole splat capable of standing on its own. If they were just a Solar variant of no particular setting significance, mirrors would've been a great idea.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It seems weird, to me, to give DBs a &quot;variant&quot; when no other exalt has a &quot;variant&quot; except in how Solars are the base for Abyssals and Infernals. Not to bring this up again, but why do Solars get a full fledged exalt type with Abyssals, but DBs only have a sub-type of DB? <br /> <br /> Lioness has it. You need to make Underworld's Elements thematically distinct and interesting, while being different from Creation's Elements, and then make the DB type based on that. Otherwise its just DBs, except with ghost fire, and ghost water. <br /> <br /> Liminals seem to follow this idea a little, now that I read it all at once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1236-loscabadrin","name":"Loscabadrin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T14:15:06-07:00","id":864520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loscabadrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/863791-are-dragon-blooded-of-a-different-color-still-a-thing?p=864497#post864497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lioness has it. You need to make Underworld's Elements thematically distinct and interesting, while being different from Creation's Elements, and then make the DB type based on that. Otherwise its just DBs, except with ghost fire, and ghost water.</div> </div> </div> </div>If deathly DB's were that distinct, I suspect they wouldn't fair much better than Anathema anywhere the Realm controls, in fact less so because they'll be squishy children when the Hunt shows up. Which is a fine concept for some <i>other </i>type of perverted DB, if you want something like that in your story. But the DoaDC were positioned as DBs that other DBs find a bit unsettling, rather than full-on abominations. This means they can still be part of the Polite Society that is so important to many types of DB game, even if they don't get invited to as many dinner parties (which is basically the same way Sorcerers are positioned).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T14:19:06-07:00","id":864524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/863791-are-dragon-blooded-of-a-different-color-still-a-thing?p=864520#post864520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If deathly DB's were that distinct, I suspect they wouldn't fair much better than Anathema anywhere the Realm controls, in fact less so because they'll be squishy children when the Hunt shows up. Which is a fine concept for some <i>other </i>type of perverted DB, if you want something like that in your story. But the DoaDC were positioned as DBs that other DBs find a bit unsettling, rather than full-on abominations. This means they can still be part of the Polite Society that is so important to many types of DB game, even if they don't get invited to as many dinner parties (which is basically the same way Sorcerers are positioned).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So... slightly unrelated but what if Dragons of a Different Color were the children of Dragonblooded ghosts? They are still Dragonblooded, use the same charms, but have a inclination for Necromancy and are really creepy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T14:20:05-07:00","id":864525,"title":"","content":"Dragons of a Different Color work better as being largely just reskins anyway. It's like playing a Beastman Solar, your powers are still the exact same, give or take a mutation, but you're interested in either A) the stories that arise from you being visibly different or B) the cool mental image of being a kung fu snakeman or a ghost-fire terrestrial. You don't need a list of Solar charms that only Ravenfolk Solars can take, you don't need a list of Terrestrial charms that only DDCs can take. Just refuff your anima as being spookyghost, and get on with the nifty stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/776-saintedphysician","name":"SaintedPhysician","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T14:42:25-07:00","id":864544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Loscabadrin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/863791-are-dragon-blooded-of-a-different-color-still-a-thing?p=864497#post864497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems weird, to me, to give DBs a &quot;variant&quot; when no other exalt has a &quot;variant&quot; except in how Solars are the base for Abyssals and Infernals. Not to bring this up again, but why do Solars get a full fledged exalt type with Abyssals, but DBs only have a sub-type of DB?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm open to the idea of variants for other Exalt types, if anyone has any good ideas.<br /> <br /> As for Abyssals, they're supposed to be very different from Solars. Underworld DBs, or Autocthonian DBs, or Vitriol DBs, are not supposed to be very different from standard DBs. They're supposed to be tweaks, not rewrites.<br /> <br /> Refluffing your anima's barely even a tweak, though.<br /> <br /> Actually changing the anima power, and the extra effects of Charms like Elemental Bolt Attack, might be a good approach for people who'd like more than aesthetics but less than new Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T16:45:00-07:00","id":864610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/863791-are-dragon-blooded-of-a-different-color-still-a-thing?p=864524#post864524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... slightly unrelated but what if Dragons of a Different Color were the children of Dragonblooded ghosts? They are still Dragonblooded, use the same charms, but have a inclination for Necromancy and are really creepy.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Ghostblooded Dragonblooded (where the ghost-parent's Breeding dominated)? I'd be tempted to save that for the &quot;really perverse&quot; case rather than DoaDC, because if it's a knowable fact that that's where these DoaDC come from, then they're inherently a crime against the natural order (from the Immaculate perspective). Although, I suppose a Dragonblooded who's tossing around Necromancy is probably <i>already</i> on the IO's shitlist. As long as the creep-FX are subtle enough that they feed <i>rumors</i> about the DoaDC's parentage rather than proving it, I suppose it could work fine.<br /> <br /> EDIT: In my headcanon DoaDC are a sympathetic symptom of the damage done to Creation's Dragon Lines by the presence of Shadowlands. They were practically unheard of in the First Age because shadowlands were so rare, but now happen much more often than anyone wants to talk about (still very rare, tho). The strong geomancy of the Blessed Isle prevents this effect somewhat, but in Lookshy they may be as common as one-in-a-hundred by now.<br /> <br /> Since Shadowlands are by far the most common type of geomantic deformity in Creation, these guys are the only type of DoaDC anyone has ever heard of. But it's interesting to think of what a Wyld-tainted (or Autochthon-tainted, or...) DB might be like too, if such a thing could possibly exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 04-12-2016, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T10:37:01-07:00","id":865587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/863791-are-dragon-blooded-of-a-different-color-still-a-thing?p=864440#post864440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't want a new splat. I just want DBs with a twist.<br /> <br /> Mirrors worked poorly because Abyssals were supposed to be a whole splat capable of standing on its own. If they were just a Solar variant of no particular setting significance, mirrors would've been a great idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually a good point. Variants wouldn't have to be as in-depth as a primary splat. It could be as simple as designing a few custom charms using the Exigents book we've been promised to give your character the right flavor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T11:36:34-07:00","id":865624,"title":"","content":"I believe the idea of Evocations based on bloodlines was mentioned earlier in the thread; that might serve as a useful base for such a &quot;taint&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}